1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,495
Placement rules decide where shapes appear, and they usually live in a file

2
00:00:05,495 --> 00:00:07,105
of a module or a theme.

3
00:00:07,105 --> 00:00:10,656
The Placements module edits the same rules from the admin.

4
00:00:10,656 --> 00:00:15,540
We'll create one, start another from a content type, and see where they're stored.

5
00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:23,870
A placement.json file belongs to a module or a theme.

6
00:00:23,870 --> 00:00:27,980
Each property is a shape type, and its value is an array of

7
00:00:27,980 --> 00:00:31,710
rules, so changing a rule means changing the project.

8
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:37,266
The Placements module keeps the same shape types and rules with the site instead.

9
00:00:37,266 --> 00:00:41,630
You edit them in the admin, and by default they're saved in the database.

10
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:48,057
When a theme or a module also places the shape, the Placements module takes precedence.

11
00:00:48,057 --> 00:00:54,040
A location in its rule replaces theirs, and its alternates and wrappers are added to theirs.

12
00:00:54,790 --> 00:00:59,545
In the Placements module, every rule of a shape type that matches applies,

13
00:00:59,545 --> 00:01:01,507
from the first to the last.

14
00:01:01,507 --> 00:01:06,500
A later place replaces an earlier one, and alternates and wrappers accumulate.

15
00:01:10,703 --> 00:01:13,725
Placements is a feature of the Placements module.

16
00:01:13,725 --> 00:01:19,273
It's listed under Tools, Features, in the Development category, so let's search for placements.

17
00:01:19,729 --> 00:01:21,192
Two features match.

18
00:01:21,192 --> 00:01:26,286
Placements adds the admin pages and saves rules in the database, while Placements

19
00:01:26,286 --> 00:01:29,682
file storage depends on it and saves them in a file.

20
00:01:29,682 --> 00:01:31,439
Let's enable Placements.

21
00:01:35,677 --> 00:01:40,611
With the feature enabled, Design, Placements lists the placements of the site.

22
00:01:40,611 --> 00:01:44,487
It's empty until you add one, so let's select Add Placement.

23
00:01:44,964 --> 00:01:47,929
A placement is a shape type and its rules.

24
00:01:47,929 --> 00:01:52,624
Let's enter MediaField_Edit, the shape of the editor of a media field.

25
00:01:53,076 --> 00:01:57,740
The rules are a JSON array in a code editor, starting with one empty rule.

26
00:01:57,740 --> 00:02:01,414
Saving it as it is shows an error, because a rule needs a

27
00:02:01,414 --> 00:02:04,096
place, a shape, wrappers, or alternates.

28
00:02:04,548 --> 00:02:08,817
Let's replace it with a rule for the Image field of the BlogPost part.

29
00:02:08,817 --> 00:02:13,647
The differentiator, BlogPost-Image, names the part and the field, and a place of

30
00:02:13,647 --> 00:02:15,108
"-" hides the shape.

31
00:02:15,595 --> 00:02:20,737
Save returns to the list, where the placement is a row named after its shape type.

32
00:02:20,737 --> 00:02:25,761
Edit reopens its rules, Delete removes the placement, and the search box filters

33
00:02:25,761 --> 00:02:27,455
the list by shape type.

34
00:02:27,953 --> 00:02:31,127
Let's check the result in the editor of a blog post.

35
00:02:31,127 --> 00:02:35,560
The Banner Image field, whose technical name is Image, is gone, because the

36
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:37,093
rule hides its editor.

37
00:02:41,307 --> 00:02:45,004
The settings of a content part, of a part in a type, and

38
00:02:45,004 --> 00:02:47,151
of a field link to placements.

39
00:02:47,151 --> 00:02:52,517
Let's open Content Types, edit the Blog Post type, and then edit its Subtitle field.

40
00:02:52,989 --> 00:02:56,105
The field settings have an Edit placements button.

41
00:02:56,105 --> 00:03:00,166
Its menu lists a placement for the field, one for detail views, one

42
00:03:00,166 --> 00:03:03,169
for summary views, and one for the admin editor.

43
00:03:03,696 --> 00:03:09,259
The editor entry opens Edit Placement with the shape type TextField_Edit, and a

44
00:03:09,259 --> 00:03:14,036
rule whose differentiator, BlogPost-Subtitle, is already filled in.

45
00:03:14,515 --> 00:03:18,355
The rule needs a place, so let's add a place of "-", which

46
00:03:18,355 --> 00:03:20,275
hides the shape, and save.

47
00:03:20,738 --> 00:03:23,098
Save returns to the field settings.

48
00:03:23,098 --> 00:03:27,818
In Design, Placements, the list holds both placements, sorted by shape type.

49
00:03:32,018 --> 00:03:36,297
A service that implements IPlacementStore loads and saves the placements.

50
00:03:36,297 --> 00:03:40,685
The module registers a database store by default, so placements are part of

51
00:03:40,685 --> 00:03:42,148
the data of the site.

52
00:03:42,898 --> 00:03:48,262
Enabling Placements file storage replaces that registration with a file store.

53
00:03:48,262 --> 00:03:55,478
The placements are then saved in PlacementsDocument.json, in the folder of the tenant under App_Data/Sites.

54
00:03:59,678 --> 00:04:04,238
In a recipe, the Placements step holds an object with one property per

55
00:04:04,238 --> 00:04:06,698
shape type, each an array of rules.

56
00:04:06,698 --> 00:04:12,638
Executing the step saves the rules of every shape type it lists, replacing the existing ones.

57
00:04:13,388 --> 00:04:18,831
With the Deployment module enabled, a deployment plan can include the All Placements step.

58
00:04:18,831 --> 00:04:22,970
It exports every placement of the site as a Placements step in this

59
00:04:22,970 --> 00:04:25,578
format, so another site can import them.

60
00:04:27,578 --> 00:04:29,526
That's the Placements module:

61
00:04:29,526 --> 00:04:33,423
the rules of a placement file, edited in the admin, saved in the

62
00:04:33,423 --> 00:04:36,930
database or a file, and moved between sites with recipes.

63
00:04:36,930 --> 00:04:38,378
Thanks for watching.

